    {
      "name": "TrackLap",
      "bundleIdentifier": "com.local.tracklap",
      "developerName": "TheBlackSide243",
      "iconURL": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheBlackSide243/feather-repo/main/icons/tracklap.png",
      "localizedDescription": "Lap, sector and live delta timing from GPS, for track days by car, motorcycle or scooter: any ESP32 with Bluetooth and a GPS (firmware installed from the browser at esp32.tbsgaming.win, with a dashboard on the Waveshare ESP32-C6-LCD-1.47, and g-forces from the accelerometer of its Touch version), the iPhone's own GPS, or a simulated car to try it right away. Worldwide track search as you type, a catalog of 60+ famous circuits and a satellite editor for the start line and sectors. Lap analysis inspired by RaceChrono: compare with any lap or your track record, one cursor across map and charts, corner speeds, where you gain and lose, sectors and a friction circle; voice lap times, GPX and CSV export. With friends: chase a friend's lap shared as a file, live groups with standings and gaps on track, online leaderboards for every circuit. Drag mode like a performance meter: 0-100, quarter mile, rolling 80-120 and 100-0 braking with a one-press start, records and the ESP32 dashboard. Picking a track places the start line and sectors by themselves, from the finish line OpenStreetMap marks where it has one. Your garage: every car with its photo, power, weight and modifications, public at a link of its own, and on the leaderboards each time shows the car and whether it came from an external GPS or the iPhone. Setups for every car, for the wet and the dry, with every earlier version kept and each session remembering the one it was driven with; Live offers the wet one when it rains at the track. Setups never go online: they leave the phone only as a file you export. On two wheels Live has a lean dial, the lap analysis a chart of the lean along the lap, and setups have preload, sag and gearing. A notification tells you when a friend sets a new record on a track. Your sessions can be shared with everyone, friends only or nobody: track, day, vehicle and lap times, never traces. TrackLap Lite, a separate free app, has the timer, Drag, tracks and sessions without an account. In Italian, English, Spanish, French, German and Portuguese.",
      "subtitle": "GPS lap timer for cars, motorcycles and scooters",
